; Bare `dune build` builds only the installable package (plugin + theories).
; Tests are built on demand via their explicit `@tests/<cat>/<name>/runtest`
; aliases (see bin/test_runner and the Makefile test targets), so known-broken
; wip tests never break a plain `dune build` / `dune install`.
; `rocq-crane.install` is listed as well as the package itself: the package
; dep builds everything that would be installed, but not the .install file
; `dune install` reads, so without it a bare `dune build && dune install`
; fails with "the following <package>.install are missing".
(alias
 (name default)
 (deps (package rocq-crane) rocq-crane.install))
